\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Now the year is crowned with blessing
\par As we gather in the grain;
\par And, our grateful thanks expressing,
\par Lord we raise a joyous strain.
\par Begone days of toil and sadness
\par Cannot now our peace destroy;
\par For the hills are clothed with gladness,
\par And the valleys shout for joy.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par To the Lord their first- fruits bringing
\par All His thankful people come,
\par To the Father praises singing
\par For the joy of harvest home.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. In the spring the smiling meadows
\par Donned their robes of living green,
\par As the sunshine chased the shadows
\par Swiftly o'er the changing scene;
\par In the summer- time the story
\par Of a riper hope was told;
\par Then the rich autumnal glory
\par Decked the fields in cloth of gold.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par To the Lord their first- fruits bringing
\par All His thankful people come,
\par To the Father praises singing
\par For the joy of harvest home.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Shall not we, whose hearts are swelling
\par With the thought of former days,
\par Sing a joyous song foretelling
\par Future gladness, fuller praise?
\par For the cloud the bow retaineth
\par With its covenant of peace,
\par That, as long as earth remaineth,
\par Harvest- time shall never cease.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par To the Lord their first- fruits bringing
\par All His thankful people come,
\par To the Father praises singing
\par For the joy of harvest home.
\par \f1 
